at's available... I don't have access to npm registry, so I'll use a reasonable version.\n\nLet me use `\"@electric-sql/pglite\": \"^0.2.0\"`.\n\nOK, let me create all the files now.\n\nActually, I realize I should also consider that the user might want to run `npm install` at the root level and have everything work. Let me structure the package.json files appropriately.\n\nRoot `package.json`:\n```json\n{\n  \"name\": \"message-board\",\n  \"version\": \"1.0.0\",\n  \"scripts\": {\n    \"dev\": \"concurrently \\\"npm run server\\\" \\\"npm run client\\\"\",\n    \"server\": \"node server/index.js\",\n    \"client\": \"npm run dev --prefix client\"\n  },\n  \"dependencies\": {\n    \"concurrently\": \"^8.2.0\"\n  }\n}\n```\n\nServer `package.json`:\n```json\n{\n  \"name\": \"message-board-server\",\n  \"version\": \"1.0.0\",\n  \"type\": \"module\",\n  \"scripts\": {\n    \"start\": \"node index.js\"\n  },\n  \"dependencies\": {\n    \"@electric-sql/pglite\": \"^0.2.0\",\n    \"cors\": \"^2.8.5\",\n    \"express\": \"^4.18.2\"\n  }\n}\n```\n\nClient `package.json`:\n```json\n{\n  \"name\": \"message-board-client\",\n  \"version\": \"1.0.0\",\n  \"type\": \"module\",\n  \"scripts\": {\n    \"dev\": \"vite\",\n    \"build\": \"vite build\",\n    \"preview\": \"vite preview\"\n  },\n  \"devDependencies\": {\n    \"vite\": \"^5.0.0\"\n  }\n}\n```\n\nNow let me create all the files.\n\nActually, I should also add a `.gitignore` file to ignore `node_modules` and `data` directories.\n\nLet me create all the files now.\n\nHmm, let me also think about the PGLite API one more time. I want to make sure I'm using the correct method names.\n\nLooking at the PGLite documentation:\n- `PGlite.create(options)` - Creates a new PGlite instance\n- `pglite.query(sql, params?)` - Executes a query and returns results\n- `pglite.exec(sql)` - Executes SQL without returning results\n\nI think my code is correct. Let me proceed.\n\nActually, I just realized that the `query` method might retur