k if there are any issues with the code...\n\nOne thing I notice is that I'm using `fileURLToPath` and `import.meta.url` which requires Node.js to be run as an ES module. The server `package.json` has `\"type\": \"module\"`, so this should work.\n\nAlso, I'm using `PGlite.create()` which is the correct API for PGLite.\n\nThe SSE implementation looks correct:\n- Sets proper headers\n- Flushes headers to start the stream\n- Maintains a list of active clients\n- Broadcasts new messages to all clients\n- Cleans up when clients disconnect\n\nThe frontend implementation looks correct:\n- Uses EventSource for SSE\n- Handles reconnection on error\n- Escapes HTML to prevent XSS\n- Fetches initial messages on load\n- Posts new messages via form submission\n\nI think everything is in order. Let me call finish.\n","tool_calls":[{"type":"function","function":{"name":"finish","arguments":"{\"summary\":\"I've implemented the complete message board application with the following structure:\\n\\n**Project Structure:**\\n```\\napp/\\n├── package.json              # Root: concurrently script to run both servers\\n├── server/\\n│   ├── package.json          # Backend: express, @electric-sql/pglite, cors\\n│   └── index.js              # Express server with PGLite and SSE\\n└── client/\\n    ├── package.json          # Frontend: vite\\n    ├── index.html            # Clean HTML layout with CSS\\n    └── src/\\n        └── main.js           # Vanilla JS: SSE, message handling\\n```\\n\\n**Backend (server/index.js):**\\n- Express server with CORS and JSON body parsing\\n- PGLite embedded database with filesystem persistence (`./data` directory)\\n- Database auto-initialization with `messages` table (id, text, created_at)\\n- `GET /api/messages` - Fetches all messages ordered by creation time\\n- `POST /api/messages` - Inserts new message and broadcasts to all SSE clients\\n- `GET /api/stream` - SSE endpoint maintaining active connections, broadcasting new messages\\n\\n**Frontend (client/